            <div xml:id="d361">

                <pb facs="0596" n="1182" sameAs="frus:frus1949v07p2/pg1182"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.001 Chiang Kai-shek/8–449: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Taipei</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Macdonald</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Taipei</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-08-04">August 4, 1949</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>351. Generalissimo left for Korea yesterday with entourage of 9 including Wang
                    Shih-chieh, Huang Shao-ku, General Yu Chih-shih and Chang Chi-yun, all members
                    of Generalissimo’s headquarters.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 351; repeated OffEmb Canton 158.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Macdonald</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
